Hi there! Thanks for stopping by 👋

Are you actively looking for a new opportunity? Or just checking the market? Well… you might just be in the right place!

We’re looking for a Lead Strategic Financial Analyst to join our Finance team across North America, reporting to the Director, Strategic Finance & Insights and working directly with the VP Finance and CFO. You will tackle complex, cross-functional business questions that require curiosity, sound judgment and a willingness to navigate ambiguity. You will work across multiple areas of the business, gaining exposure to different business models, revenue streams and strategic priorities. You will take on questions that require you to connect the dots, build analysis from the ground up and bring a clear point of view to senior leadership.

Please note: This role is open across (Location) and requires you to be available to work within EST/EDT hours.

What you’ll be doing:

- Take on complex, open-ended questions that span multiple parts of the business and bring structure to ambiguity;

- Understand how our different businesses make money, identify the key drivers of growth, and assess whether that growth is sustainable, connecting the individual business performance to the broader consolidated picture;

- Build financial models and analysis from the ground up to answer strategic questions and support business decisions;

- Find, access and validate the data you need, including working directly with SQL and BI tools when the answer isn’t readily available;

- Improve forecasting across the business, both in-year and long-range, by strengthening methodologies and key drivers, increasing accuracy, and making the process more efficient and easier to explain;

- Own the monthly and quarterly finance rhythm, partnering closely with business teams on reviews and reporting while maintaining a consistent standard across all areas of the business;

- Challenge assumptions, identify risks and opportunities, and turn complex analysis into clear recommendations for the Director, Strategic Finance & Insights, VP Finance, CFO and business leaders.

What you need to bring:

We’re a team within Finance responsible for helping Lightspeed understand what is driving our business today, where it is going next, and what we should do about it. This role sits at the intersection of strategic finance, data and business analysis, with exposure across Lightspeed’s software, payments, capital and hardware businesses.

- Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to bring structure to ambiguous or unowned problems;

- Sound financial modelling skills, including building driver-based models and three-statement analysis from the ground up;

- Experience working with data directly, including SQL or an equivalent querying tool and a BI platform;

- Strong business curiosity and the ability to dig into a number until you understand what is really driving it;

- The ability to challenge assumptions and numbers while building trusted relationships with business partners;

- Strong communication skills, with the ability to make complex analysis clear and actionable for both finance and non-finance audiences;

- Experience working in a complex business with multiple revenue streams or business models.

You’ll enjoy:

- A flexible work environment that empowers you to do your best work

- A culture that celebrates performance

- The chance to make an impact in a team that’s big enough for career growth, but lean enough to make your voice heard

- Career-defining opportunities

Plus benefits designed to keep you happy, healthy and fulfilled.

- Flexible paid time off and remote work policies

- Equity options, because this is your company too

- Contributions to your pension plan. Your future matters

- Training opportunities to grow your skills and career

- Health and wellness credit so you feel your best

- Time off to volunteer and give back to your community

- Interest groups, employee led networks, socia

Please note that this position is fully remote. That said, if you are based in Poland, Portugal, or Ukraine, you are welcome to use our local offices whenever it suits you.
About the role
PandaDoc is hiring its first Design Engineer to sit at the intersection of design and engineering in the Embedded Agreements track. You'll own the design of two strategic areas - our API and our integrations - the surfaces that connect PandaDoc to the broader ecosystem of tools our customers already work in.
The Embedded Agreements track is where PandaDoc extends beyond the product itself. Our API is where developers build on top of PandaDoc , embed document workflows into their own products, and connect to AI-native environments - including our ChatGPT app, Claude connector, and MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration. Our integrations area is where users connect PandaDoc to the tools they already use, like Salesforce and HubSpot, to automate document workflows across their stack.
And the ground is shifting. The technical barrier to working with programmatic surfaces like our API is falling fast: MCP and AI surfaces like Claude and ChatGPT are collapsing the effort it takes to connect to an API or an MCP server. That means the audience for these surfaces is no longer just developers - it's a larger and growing group whose expectations are changing as quickly as the way developers themselves now build. We're looking for someone who can partner closely with product to help define our strategy here, stay close to how the market is moving, and let that shape how we design these surfaces for an expanding audience.
Both areas are technically complex and require someone who can hold the developer experience and the end-user experience in mind at the same time. This is a role for someone who has the eye of a designer, understands and can ship code, and is genuinely excited about building for developers and an increasingly broad set of power users. You will own a strategic area end to end. We expect you to be opinionated, deeply curious about how people and tools interact, and comfortable shaping a product area with limited prior template.
What you'll do

• Own the design of our API and integrations areas end to end - from developer-facing API surfaces and documentation experiences to the in-product flows users rely on to connect their tools;

• Partner with product and research to shape strategy for these surfaces - staying close to how the market and the audience are shifting as the barrier to working with APIs and MCP falls, and translating that into how we design for a broader, evolving set of users;

• Design and prototype AI-native patterns for our API - including our ChatGPT app, Claude connector, and MCP integration - surfaces where PandaDoc meets AI assistants and agentic workflows;

• Shape how integrations feel across the product, with intent around two questions in particular: how our core CRM integrations (Salesforce, HubSpot) need to adapt for an agentic world, and how we balance the integrations we build ourselves against the connections customers orchestrate for themselves in surfaces like Claude via MCP - when each makes sense, when a hybrid is right, and how to design an experience that intentionally guides customers to the best option for them;

• Prototype ideas in code, fast. Take a concept from Figma or an LLM conversation to a working production-grade React component in days, owning layout, interaction, accessibility, and performance;

• Trailblaze the Design Engineer function at PandaDoc . Own work end to end, from problem framing to launch, and shape how this role operates as the first hire in it;

• As the only Design Engineer on the Embedded Agreements team, bring your technical perspective into the design process - sharing patterns, pairing on prototypes, and helping the designers around you improve their technical skills over time;

